h Jojo Phillips in the back of the end zone in the third overtime, helping No. 10 BYU beat Kansas to keep its CFP hopes alive.","published":"2026-11-21T21:39:12.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50553754/byu-retains-cfp-hopes-beats-kansas-triple-over","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Nebraska snaps AP Top 25 losing skid, upsets Ohio State","description":"Nebraska broke its 31-game losing streak against AP Top 25 opponents with a 31-28 victory over No. 16 Ohio State on Saturday.","published":"2026-11-21T21:11:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50553426/nebraska-snaps-ap-top-25-losing-skid-upsets-ohio-state","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Nebraska's Matt Rhule ends his drought against ranked opponents","description":"Rhule and Nebraska brought an end to the Cornhuskers coach's infamous decade-long streak against Ohio State.","published":"2026-11-21T20:58:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50534102/nebraska-cornhuskers-matt-rhule-ranked-win-drought","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Syracuse QB Steve Angeli exits with injury, arm in sling","description":"Syracuse senior quarterback Steve Angeli left Saturday's game against Boston College with an injury to his throwing arm and will not return.","published":"2026-11-21T20:51:03.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50552810/syracuse-qb-steve-angeli-exits-injury-arm-sling","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Jake Trotter","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Week 12 live: Tracking top moments and best highlights","description":"Tracking the top plays and developments from Week 12.","published":"2026-11-21T18:35:28.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50541394/week-12-live-highlights","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Army pulls seating prank at Navy's football stadium ahead of Memphis game","description":"The letters were adjusted back in time for Navy's kickoff.","published":"2026-11-21T18:47:15.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50551457/army-navy-seat-prank","type":"Story","byline":"Associated Press","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Keisean Henderson leads Houston to win after QB Conner Weigman ruled out","description":"Houston ruled out starting QB Conner Weigman vs. West Virginia due to injury and instead went with true freshman Keisean Henderson, the No. 4 recruit for 2026.","published":"2026-11-21T21:38:48.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50550966/sources-houston-qb-conner-weigman-henderson-start","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Which teams have the best odds to make the College Football Playoff?","description":"We are tracking the odds for making the CFP, earning a bye and winning it all.","published":"2026-11-21T16:04:07.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50532919/college-football-playoff-odds-predictions","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"What are the conference title game clinching scenarios for Week 12?","description":"Here's what teams from every conference would need to play for their league championship.","published":"2026-11-21T16:00:59.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50512475/conference-title-game-clinching-scenarios-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Michigan starts QB Bryce Underwood vs. UCLA; Andrew Marsh suspended","description":"Michigan started QB Bryce Underwood over Tommy Carr, who had started the past four games. WR Andrew Marsh, meanwhile, is suspended for Saturday's game vs. UCLA.","published":"2026-11-21T20:46:38.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50549879/sources-michigan-expected-start-bryce-underwood-vs-ucla","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5136784/francis-brewu","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francis_Brewu"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Francis Brewu","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francis_Brewu","description":"American football player (born 2006)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:30Z","intro":"Francis Brewu (born January 17, 2006) is an American college football defensive tackle for the Notre Dame Fighting Irish. He previously played for the Pittsburgh Panthers.","sections":[{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"In January 2024, Brewu enrolled early at Pittsburgh. He quickly impressed during spring camp due to his size and technique and was moved off of the scout team. He was also named the strongest player on the team by his teammates. Prior to the 2024 season, Brewu was named number 77 on Bruce Feldman’s Freaks List. During the season he played in 12 games with one start and totaled 15 tackles, three tackles for loss and 1.5 sacks. He was also named to the Pro Football Focus (PFF) All-Freshman Team at the end of the season. In December 2024, Brewu announced he would return to the Panthers for 2025. On August 4, 2025, Brewu was again named to Feldman's Freaks List, this time at number 24. In 2025 Brewu started 12 games for the Panthers in which he led all Pitt interior defensive linemen in tackles. Due to his performance, Brewu gained recognition as an Honorable Mention All-ACC selection. On January 6, 2026, Brewu entered the transfer portal, and chose to transfer to the Notre Dame Fighting Irish on January 13. On August 10, 2026, Brewu was named to Bruce Feldman’s Freaks List for the third consecutive season."}]}}